# Lander — our marketing site, as a workbook

Our public landing page, migrated from the old `web/index.html` god-file into a **folder of `.work`
sections** — each its own file with the reasoning in prose and the UI in a `client` block. The nexus
composes them into one page; the shared look lives in `design.work`; the behavior in `99-scripts.work`;
the brand assets (fonts, icons) travel with the workbook and are served as static files.

The site *is* a workbook now — no SvelteKit, no build pipeline, no god-file. Each section reads on its
own, and the whole thing is one mount on our nexus, alongside docs/cloud/waitlist/marketing.

## The sections

- **01-hero** — the promise + CTAs, over the lattice animation.
- **02-platforms** — build on desktop, ship to cloud.
- **03-cloud-pricing** — storage + usage, never seats.
- **04-what-is-a-workbook** — the atom of a living internet.
- **05-s3** — the closing build.
- **06-modal** — notify-me, captured into our waitlist workbook.

The original `web/index.html` stays until this is verified at full parity.
